# Build and Release

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2 and later
Dependencies: `01_PROJECT_FOUNDATION.todo`, `12_TESTING_PERFORMANCE_TOOLING.todo`

## Purpose

Produce reproducible, identifiable, validated builds without committing generated artifacts.

## Tasks

- [ ] Define development and release build profiles.
- [ ] Define versioning policy.
- [ ] Embed commit and build metadata.
- [x] Validate required scenes.
- [ ] Validate configuration and licenses.
- [x] Create clean build output directory outside tracked assets.
- [x] Create one-command development build.
- [ ] Create one-command test-plus-build workflow.
- [ ] Document supported PC environment.
- [ ] Create artifact manifest.
- [ ] Create release checklist.
- [ ] Define rollback and patch process before public release.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Clean checkout can produce a development build.
- [ ] Build identifies version and source commit.
- [ ] Generated artifacts remain untracked.
- [ ] Failed validation stops the build.
- [ ] Artifact manifest lists build, tests, known issues, and licenses.

## Completion evidence

Foundation evidence:

- Bootstrap is the enabled build scene.
- `EntropyTag.Editor.EntropyTagBuildCommand.BuildWindowsDevelopment` fails if no scene is enabled.
- `scripts/Invoke-UnityBuild.ps1` creates an ignored Windows development build and verifies the executable.
- The generated executable remained alive during an 8-second launch smoke test.

## Completion log

- 2026-08-19 - Added the first validated one-command Windows development build. Version metadata,
  test-plus-build orchestration, artifact manifests, release profiles, and release policy remain outstanding.
